1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Light striking the photocathode releases an electron.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,300
A high voltage applied between successive electrodes

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,100
accelerates the electron toward the next electrode,

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:17,800
multiplying the number of electrons at every stage.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:24,000
The resulting electrical signal can be amplified by a million to a hundred million times.
